  "description": "The deployment guide's backup procedure accounts for the data root's scratch directory, so a backup carries no pending redo record.\n\n## Background\n\nThe guide tells the reader to archive the whole data root and restore it elsewhere. Under the redo record that captures a pending commit point: restoring it into a repository that never performed the mutation would apply the record at the next session open.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: The backup procedure excludes the data root's scratch directory.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The restore procedure states that a restored data root carries no pending record.\n- [hard] REQ-03: The guide states why the scratch directory is excluded, in one sentence.\n- [hard] REQ-04: The guide carries no description of journaled publication.\n",
